{
  "about": "How the field uses the meadow sheets. sheets: PNG files in one of two layouts, 3 x 5 (ground) or 3 x 2 (objects), and a frame name per tile in reading order (rows by the tiles' feet, left to right; null skips). mirror: new frame -> frame mirrored left-right (swaps the grid axes). terrain: frames per server terrain, one picked per tile by position (repeat a name to weight it); water and the like may split into edge and inner (inner = all four neighbours the same terrain) and add shore: pieces by where the other terrain is (ul = -x, ur = -y, lr = +x, ll = +y; corners top, right, bottom, left). bank: water terrain -> pieces for a land tile beside it, by the side the water is on. node: frames that replace the ground of a flat tile holding that resource node. marker: obstacles drawn as marker_ground with the placeholder mark on top. filler: the block stacked under raised tiles; block_levels: height levels one block covers.",
